//! Sigil Self-Hosted Compiler
//!
//! This is the beginning of the Sigil compiler written in Sigil itself.
//! Part of the Jormungandr research initiative - the self-hosting bootstrap.
//!
//! ## Module Structure
//!
//! - `span` - Source location tracking
//! - `token` - Token definitions for the lexer
//! - `ast` - Abstract Syntax Tree definitions
//! - `lexer` - Tokenization
//!
//! ## Status
//!
//! Phase 4: Frontend implementation (IN PROGRESS)
//! - [x] span.sg - Source span tracking
//! - [x] token.sg - Token definitions
//! - [x] ast.sg - AST node definitions
//! - [x] lexer.sg - Tokenization
//! - [ ] parser.sg - Parsing
//! - [ ] typeck.sg - Type checking
//! - [ ] ir.sg - Intermediate representation
//! - [ ] lower.sg - AST to IR lowering
//!
//! ## Bootstrap Strategy
//!
//! 1. Define core data structures in Sigil (COMPLETE)
//! 2. Implement lexer and parser in Sigil (IN PROGRESS)
//! 3. Implement type checker with evidentiality
//! 4. Implement IR and code generation
//! 5. Achieve self-hosting: Sigil compiles Sigil
//!
//! ## Evidentiality in the Compiler
//!
//! The self-hosted compiler uses Sigil's evidentiality system:
//! - `!` (Known) - Verified compiler-internal values
//! - `?` (Uncertain) - User-provided input that may be invalid
//! - `~` (Reported) - Values from external sources (files, etc.)
//!
//! This dogfooding ensures the evidentiality system is practical.

// Core modules
pub mod span;
pub mod token;
pub mod ast;
pub mod lexer;

// Re-exports for convenience
pub use span::{Span, Spanned};
pub use token::{Token, SpannedToken};
pub use ast::*;
pub use lexer::Lexer;

/// Compiler version
pub const VERSION: !&str = "0.1.0-bootstrap";

/// Check if we're in bootstrap mode
pub const BOOTSTRAP: !bool = true;
